{"id": "EUVD-2026-78467", "enisaUuid": "e323e622-ae78-3f93-9d7a-3b84f6ad5c78", "description": "On macOS, the virtio-fs host server used by Docker Sandboxes improperly follows symlinks when reopening an unlinked file from a stored path. A malicious guest can replace a parent directory with a symlink, escape the shared workspace, and read or modify arbitrary host files as the VMM user, potentially achieving host code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-09-15T13:32:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-15T21:43:07", "baseScore": 9.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/", "https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/isolation/", "https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/releases/tag/v0.42.0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4x2g-7mfh-8rx6", "CVE-2026-77179"], "assigner": "Docker", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "43389cca-9417-3846-8945-0740b6b1f2a9", "product": {"name": "Docker Sandboxes", "vendor": {"name": "Docker"}}, "product_version": "0.28.0 <0.42.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "72e80b53-00d4-3b7b-be64-87311d07f992", "vendor": {"name": "Docker"}}], "isExploited": false}